* TK_AI
* The full-screen toolkit, shared base: the AI line, the preview, the wait and the answer (S.69, plan .claude/plan-fullscreen-toolkit.md 2.9 and
* .claude/ai-integration-evaluation.md 5B; the owner's D4a answer of 20 Oct 2026: "a one line ai entry field at the bottom of each form with the response in a
* popup window", and of 23 Oct: the AI line turns a request into one of the page's own actions).
* Copyright (c) 2026, SD Core for Linux.  This program is free software; you can redistribute
* it and/or modify it under the terms of the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later.
*
* START-HISTORY:
* 23 Oct 26 dm  New (AI line stage 1: the library routine and the home screen).
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   call $tk_ai(op, ctx, a, b)
*
*   init    (ctx)              asks the helper (KERNEL K$AI.STATUS) whether the AI is usable for this account: the gate is on and a provider, a model and a key are
*                              set.  Sets ctx<TK.C.AI> to 1 when it is and makes the line; else the line is NOT DRAWN AT ALL (the owner, 20 Oct: an account without the AI
*                              sees no AI bar).  The app calls it after $tk_open and again when the account changes.
*   draw    (ctx, focused)     draws the line on row YSTAT - 1: the label, then the entry; empty and not focused it shows a dim hint.
*   key     (ctx, nm -> out)   a key for the line while it has the focus: Esc gives the focus back (out 'leave'); Tab, Shift-Tab, Up and Down also give it back and come back
*                              as out 'tab' 'btab' 'up' 'down' for the app to move its own focus; Enter on a non-empty line is out 'ask'; any other key edits the line (the
*                              library's entry widget: left, right, home, end, delete, ctrl-u ...).
*   focus   (ctx, on)          gives the line the focus (1) or takes it away (0) and draws it.
*   mouse   (ctx, mev -> out)  out 'focus' when a press of the left button lands on the line.
*   text    (ctx -> out)       the line's text.
*   clear   (ctx)              empties the line.
*   usable  (-> a, b)          for an app that has no line of its own on the toolkit's frame (the IDE puts an entry in its own form): a is 1 when the AI is usable for this account
*                              (the same four tests as init), and b is the provider and the model, as two fields.
*   ask     (ctx, actx -> res) THE WHOLE SEQUENCE for the request in the line: the preview (everything that will leave the machine, Send or Cancel, Cancel is the
*                              default), the sending, the wait (Esc gives it up), the answer, the proposal and Accept / Reject.  Nothing is sent unless Send is chosen.
*                              An app without the line passes the request in actx<6>, and ctx needs only TK.C.W.
*
*   actx is what the app tells the model, one dynamic array: <1> the app's name; <2> the kind (a word for the prompt); <3> text about the page, its lines separated by VALUE marks (the app
*   decides; no data values); <4> the actions the app offers, VALUES of 'id:what it does'; <5> 1 when every action only NAVIGATES (opens a tool the person could open anyway), in which
*   case Enter alone accepts the proposal (the owner's answer of 23 Oct), else 0 and Enter alone rejects.  res is: <1> 'none', 'action' or 'command'; <2> the action's id or the command;
*   <3> the action's argument (letters, digits and . _ : / space - only); <4> what the AI said; <5> a line for the app's status bar (a failure, or that it was given up).
*
*   FOR AN APP THAT WORKS ON TEXT (the IDE; stage 2, 23 Oct 26) actx has more: <6> the request, when the app has no line to take it from; <7> the screen row on which the wait is written; <8> THE TEXT
*   being worked on, its lines joined with a line feed (at most 24000 bytes: the app cuts it); <9> the number of its first line; <10> the SELECTED text, lines joined with a line feed;
*   <11> 'nocmd' when the app has nowhere to run a command, which makes the library ignore one.  The text is sent as it is, a byte that is not plain ASCII shown to the model as ?
*   (one for one, so a position in what it saw is a position in the original).  The model may then answer with "edits": a list of {"old", "new"}.  Each old must be in the text EXACTLY ONCE,
*   in whole lines or not, the edits must not overlap, there are at most 8 and the original must really hold what the model was shown at that place.  A set that does not meet that is ignored
*   whole and said so (11660).  A set that is accepted is SHOWN as a diff in full - the line numbers, the old lines with -, the new lines with + - and a diff of more than 30 lines is not
*   offered (11659), so that nobody accepts what they could not read.  The default button is Reject.  res is then <1> 'edit', <2> the edits, as values of  position SM length SM new text
*   (positions in the text of actx<8>, in the order they appear), <4> what the AI said.  THE LIBRARY CHANGES NOTHING: the app applies an accepted set to its own buffer, through its own
*   undo, and saves nothing.
*
*   WHAT THE MODEL CAN CAUSE.  It returns text.  The text is read as ONE JSON object: say (shown), action (used only if it is exactly one of the ids the app offered), arg (cleaned) and
*   command (printable ASCII, 200 characters, shown for the person to run or reject; this routine never runs it).  Anything else is ignored and said so.  The app performs an accepted
*   action itself, through its own code, so its own gates decide.  The audit line is the kernel's, written before the request goes (K$AI.START): program tk_ai.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
subroutine tk_ai(op, ctx, a, b)
$catalog $tk_ai

$include keys.h
$include int$keys.h
$include err.h
$include sl.h
$include tk.h

   common /tkai/ ai.on, ai.w, ai.focus, ai.prov, ai.model, ai.line

   if unassigned(ai.on) then
      ai.on = 0
      ai.w = ''
      ai.focus = 0
      ai.prov = ''
      ai.model = ''
      ai.line = 0
   end

   begin case
      case op = 'usable'
         gosub read.status
         ai.line = 0                                      ;* this app draws no line of the library's (a line left by an earlier app of the session is not this app's)
         a = ai.on
         b = ai.prov : @fm : ai.model
      case op = 'init'
         gosub read.status
         ai.line = ai.on
         ai.focus = 0
         ctx<TK.C.AI> = (if ai.on then 1 else '')
         ai.w = collection()
         if ai.on then gosub make.widget
      case op = 'draw'
         ai.focus = (a = 1)
         if ai.on then gosub paint
      case op = 'focus'
         ai.focus = (a = 1)
         if ai.on then gosub paint
      case op = 'key'
         b = ''
         if ai.on then
            nm = a
            gosub on.key
         end
      case op = 'mouse'
         b = ''
         if ai.on then
            if a<1> = 'press' and a<2> = 1 and a<4> = ctx<TK.C.YSTAT> - 1 then b = 'focus'
         end
      case op = 'text'
         a = ''
         if ai.on then a = ai.w{'value'}
      case op = 'clear'
         if ai.on then
            ai.w{'value'} = ''
            ai.w{'pos'} = 1
            ai.w{'pan'} = 1
            gosub paint
         end
      case op = 'ask'
         b = 'none'
         if ai.on then gosub run.ask
      case op = 'select'
         gosub make.select
      case op = 'window'
         gosub make.window
      case op = 'splice'
         gosub splice.edits
   end case
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- the text window and the accepted edits (shared by every editor)

* In: ctx = the lines of the text, joined with field marks; a = the mark's line, the mark's column, the cursor's line and the cursor's column, as values.  Out: b = the text between the
* mark and the cursor (the earlier end first; the character under the later end is not in it), its lines joined with a line feed <1>, and the number of its first line <2> and of its last <3>;
* null when there is no mark or nothing between.
make.select:
   t.my = a<1, 1> + 0
   t.mx = a<1, 2> + 0
   t.cy = a<1, 3> + 0
   t.cx = a<1, 4> + 0
   b = ''
   if t.my < 1 or t.mx < 1 then return
   if t.my < t.cy or (t.my = t.cy and t.mx <= t.cx) then
      t.y1 = t.my ; t.x1 = t.mx ; t.y2 = t.cy ; t.x2 = t.cx
   end else
      t.y1 = t.cy ; t.x1 = t.cx ; t.y2 = t.my ; t.x2 = t.mx
   end
   t.sel = ''
   for t.q = t.y1 to t.y2
      t.ln = ctx<t.q>
      begin case
         case t.y1 = t.y2
            t.part = t.ln[t.x1, t.x2 - t.x1]
         case t.q = t.y1
            t.part = t.ln[t.x1, 99999]
         case t.q = t.y2
            t.part = t.ln[1, t.x2 - 1]
         case 1
            t.part = t.ln
      end case
      t.sel := (if t.q = t.y1 then '' else char(10)) : t.part
   next t.q
   if t.sel = '' then return
   b = t.sel : @fm : t.y1 : @fm : t.y2
   return

* In: ctx = the lines of the text, joined with field marks; a = the cursor's line.  Out: b = the first line of the window <1>, the last <2>, the number of characters before the window in
* the whole text (a line feed after each line) <3> and the window's text, its lines joined with a line feed and a mark in a line shown as ? <4>.  The whole text when it is under 24000
* bytes, else the lines round the cursor.
make.window:
   w.lines = ctx
   w.cy = a + 0
   w.total = dcount(w.lines, @fm)
   w.first = 1
   w.last = w.total
   if len(w.lines) > 24000 then
      w.first = w.cy - 150
      if w.first < 1 then w.first = 1
      w.last = w.first
      w.size = 0
      loop
      while w.last <= w.total and w.size + len(w.lines<w.last>) + 1 <= 24000
         w.size += len(w.lines<w.last>) + 1
         w.last += 1
      repeat
      w.last -= 1
      if w.last < w.first then w.last = w.first
   end
   w.off = 0
   for w.q = 1 to w.first - 1
      w.off += len(w.lines<w.q>) + 1
   next w.q
   w.win = ''
   for w.q = w.first to w.last
      w.win := (if w.q = w.first then '' else char(10)) : w.lines<w.q>
   next w.q
   w.win = convert(@vm : @sm : @tm, '???', w.win)
   b = w.first : @fm : w.last : @fm : w.off : @fm : w.win[1, 24000]
   return

* In: ctx = the text now, its lines joined with a line feed; a = the window as make.window gave it (<1> to <4>) and <5> the accepted edits, as res<2> of 'ask' has them (values of
* position SM length SM new text, positions in the window).  Out: b = the new text <1>, the number of the first line changed <2> and the number of edits <3>; null when the text no longer
* holds, at every place, exactly what the model was shown (the person changed it while the AI answered): then nothing is to be applied.  The caller puts b<1> in its buffer.
splice.edits:
   s.now = ctx
   s.off = a<3> + 0
   s.win = a<4>
   s.ed = a<5>
   s.n = dcount(s.ed, @vm)
   s.fits = (s.n > 0)
   for s.k = 1 to s.n
      s.p = s.ed<1, s.k, 1> + 0
      s.l = s.ed<1, s.k, 2> + 0
      if s.now[s.off + s.p, s.l] # s.win[s.p, s.l] then s.fits = 0
   next s.k
   b = ''
   if not(s.fits) then return
   s.new = s.now
   for s.k = s.n to 1 step -1
      s.p = s.ed<1, s.k, 1> + 0
      s.l = s.ed<1, s.k, 2> + 0
      s.new = s.new[1, s.off + s.p - 1] : s.ed<1, s.k, 3> : s.new[s.off + s.p + s.l, 99999999]
   next s.k
   s.p1 = s.ed<1, 1, 1> + 0
   s.line1 = 1
   if s.off + s.p1 > 1 then s.line1 = count(s.now[1, s.off + s.p1 - 1], char(10)) + 1
   b = s.new : @fm : s.line1 : @fm : s.n
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- whether the AI is usable, and the line

* The helper's status line: usable only when the gate is on for this account and a provider, a model and a key are set.  Any doubt is "not usable": the line is not drawn.
read.status:
   ai.on = 0
   ai.prov = ''
   ai.model = ''
   if system(25) then return
   rp = kernel(K$AI.STATUS, 0)
   if rp<1> # 'D' then return
   hj = jparse(rp<2>)
   if status() then return
   if hj{'t'} # 'status' then return
   if not(hj{'gate'}) then return
   if hj{'provider'} = '' or hj{'model'} = '' then return
   if not(hj{'key'}) then return
   ai.prov = hj{'provider'}
   ai.model = hj{'model'}
   ai.on = 1
   return

make.widget:
   lw = ctx<TK.C.W>
   ai.label = sysmsg(11636) : ' '
   ai.w{'ax'} = 3 + len(ai.label)
   ai.w{'ay'} = ctx<TK.C.YSTAT> - 1
   ai.w{'w'} = lw - 3 - len(ai.label) - 3
   ai.w{'maxlen'} = 300
   ai.w{'value'} = ''
   call $sl_entry('init', ai.w, '', '', r)
   return

paint:
   lw = ctx<TK.C.W>
   y = ctx<TK.C.YSTAT> - 1
   keep.cur = ''
   call $sl_curat('get', keep.cur)
   ai.label = sysmsg(11636) : ' '
   screen text '' at 0,y width lw
   screen text ai.label at 3,y attr (if ai.focus then 'bold' else 'disabled')
   if ai.w{'value'} = '' and not(ai.focus) then
      screen text sysmsg(11637)[1, lw - 3 - len(ai.label) - 3] at ai.w{'ax'},y attr 'disabled'
   end else
      ai.w{'focused'} = (if ai.focus then 1 else 0)
      call $sl_scr('get', scr)
      call $sl_entry('draw', ai.w, scr, '', r)
      call $sl_scr('put', scr)
   end
   if not(ai.focus) then call $sl_curat('back', keep.cur)
   return

on.key:
   begin case
      case nm = 'esc'
         ai.focus = 0
         gosub paint
         b = 'leave'
      case nm = 'tab' or nm = 'btab' or nm = 'up' or nm = 'down'
         ai.focus = 0
         gosub paint
         b = nm
      case nm = 'enter'
         if trim(ai.w{'value'}) # '' then b = 'ask'
      case 1
         ai.w{'focused'} = 1
         call $sl_scr('get', scr)
         call $sl_entry('key', ai.w, scr, nm, r)
         call $sl_scr('put', scr)
   end case
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- the whole sequence

run.ask:
   lw = ctx<TK.C.W>
   y = ctx<TK.C.YSTAT> - 1
   if a<7> # '' then y = a<7> + 0
   if a<6> # '' then
      raw = a<6>                                          ;* an app without the line passes the request
   end else
      raw = ai.w{'value'}
   end
   gosub clean
   req = trim(clean.out)
   if req = '' then return
   app = a<1>
   no.cmd = (a<11> = 'nocmd')
   * the text being worked on, as the model will see it: a byte that is not plain ASCII (the line feed excepted) becomes ?, ONE FOR ONE, so a position in it is a position in the original
   tb.raw = a<8>[1, 24000]
   tb.first = a<9> + 0
   if tb.first < 1 then tb.first = 1
   raw = tb.raw
   gosub map1
   tbm = map.out
   raw = a<10>[1, 24000]
   gosub map1
   selm = map.out
   acts = ''
   for i = 1 to dcount(a<4>, @vm)
      raw = a<4, i>                                       ;* the app's own words, cleaned all the same: a label may be text a person typed
      gosub clean
      acts<1, i> = trim(clean.out)[1, 120]
   next i
   nav = a<5>
   n.acts = dcount(acts, @vm)

   * what will leave the machine: the fixed instruction, the list of the page's actions, what the page tells about itself, and the request
   sysx = sysmsg(11635, app)
   if tbm # '' then sysx := ' ' : sysmsg(11653)             ;* the model may answer with edits, only when there is a text to edit
   nl = char(10)
   alist = ''
   for i = 1 to n.acts
      alist := nl : '  ' : acts<1, i>
   next i
   raw = change(a<3>, @vm, nl)
   gosub clean
   ptext = clean.out
   prompt = 'Actions this page offers (id: what it does):' : alist : nl : nl : 'What this page tells you about itself:' : nl : ptext
   if tbm # '' then prompt := nl : nl : 'The text being worked on (it starts at line ' : tb.first : '):' : nl : tbm
   if selm # '' then prompt := nl : nl : 'The selected text:' : nl : selm
   prompt := nl : nl : 'Request: ' : req
   size = len(sysx) + len(prompt)

   * the preview: everything, then Send or Cancel; Cancel is what Enter chooses
   call $sl_scr('get', scr)
   wrapw = scr<SL.S.W> - 16
   if wrapw > 100 then wrapw = 100
   if wrapw < 20 then wrapw = 20
   body = sysmsg(11628, ai.prov, ai.model, size)
   body<-1> = ''
   body<-1> = sysmsg(11640, len(sysx))
   call $tk_wrap(sysx, wrapw, pieces)
   for p = 1 to dcount(pieces, @fm)
      body<-1> = '  ' : pieces<p>
   next p
   body<-1> = sysmsg(11641, n.acts, len(alist))
   for i = 1 to n.acts
      body<-1> = '  ' : acts<1, i>[1, wrapw - 2]
   next i
   body<-1> = sysmsg(11642, len(ptext))
   n.shown = dcount(ptext, nl)
   for p = 1 to n.shown
      if p <= 8 then body<-1> = '  ' : field(ptext, nl, p)[1, wrapw - 2]
   next p
   if n.shown > 8 then body<-1> = '  ' : sysmsg(11644, n.shown - 8)
   if tbm # '' then
      n.tb = dcount(tbm, nl)
      body<-1> = sysmsg(11668, n.tb, len(tbm), tb.first)
      for p = 1 to n.tb
         if p <= 6 then body<-1> = '  ' : field(tbm, nl, p)[1, wrapw - 2]
      next p
      if n.tb > 6 then body<-1> = '  ' : sysmsg(11644, n.tb - 6)
   end
   if selm # '' then
      n.sel = dcount(selm, nl)
      body<-1> = sysmsg(11669, len(selm))
      for p = 1 to n.sel
         if p <= 6 then body<-1> = '  ' : field(selm, nl, p)[1, wrapw - 2]
      next p
      if n.sel > 6 then body<-1> = '  ' : sysmsg(11644, n.sel - 6)
   end
   body<-1> = sysmsg(11643, len(req))
   call $tk_wrap(req, wrapw, pieces)
   for p = 1 to dcount(pieces, @fm)
      body<-1> = '  ' : pieces<p>
   next p
   screen msgbox body title sysmsg(11639) buttons '&Send,&Cancel' default 2 returning bn else bn = 0
   if bn # 1 then
      b = 'none' : @fm : '' : @fm : '' : @fm : '' : @fm : sysmsg(11630)
      return
   end

   * the request goes: the kernel writes the audit line first, then connects
   rq = kernel(K$AI.START, sysx : @fm : 600 : @fm : prompt)
   if rq<1> # 'OK' then
      note = (if rq<2> = 'nohelper' then sysmsg(11607) else sysmsg(11627, rq<2>, ''))
      b = 'none' : @fm : '' : @fm : '' : @fm : '' : @fm : note
      return
   end

   * the wait: Esc gives it up, so does an input that has ended or the cursor lock's own way out
   loop
      rp = kernel(K$AI.POLL, 0)
      if rp<1> # 'W' then exit
      screen text sysmsg(11645) at 3,y attr 'bold' width lw - 6
      nm = ''
      screen key timeout 1 returning nm
      gave.up = 0
      if nm = 'esc' or nm = 'guardquit' then gave.up = 1
      if nm = '' then
         if status() = ER$EOF then gave.up = 1
      end
      if gave.up then
         void kernel(K$AI.CANCEL, 0)
         b = 'none' : @fm : '' : @fm : '' : @fm : '' : @fm : sysmsg(11646)
         if ai.line then gosub paint
         return
      end
   repeat
   if ai.line then gosub paint

   * the answer: the helper's line, then the model's text as ONE JSON object
   if rp<1> # 'D' then
      b = 'none' : @fm : '' : @fm : '' : @fm : '' : @fm : sysmsg(11627, rp<2>, '')
      return
   end
   hj = jparse(rp<2>)
   if status() then
      b = 'none' : @fm : '' : @fm : '' : @fm : '' : @fm : sysmsg(11627, 'badreply', '')
      return
   end
   if hj{'t'} # 'ok' then
      code = hj{'code'}
      begin case
         case code = 'disabled'
            note = sysmsg(11624)
         case code = 'nogate'
            note = sysmsg(11625, @who)
         case code = 'nomodel'
            note = sysmsg(11626, ai.prov, 'model')
         case code = 'nokey'
            note = sysmsg(11626, ai.prov, 'key')
         case 1
            raw = hj{'msg'}
            gosub clean
            note = sysmsg(11627, code, clean.out[1, 100])
      end case
      b = 'none' : @fm : '' : @fm : '' : @fm : '' : @fm : note
      return
   end
   raw = hj{'text'}
   gosub clean
   atext = clean.out
   tok.in = hj{'in'}
   tok.out = hj{'out'}
   gosub read.proposal

   * the popup: what the AI said, the proposal if there is one, and Accept / Reject
   call $tk_wrap(say, wrapw, pieces)
   body = ''
   for p = 1 to dcount(pieces, @fm)
      body<-1> = pieces<p>
   next p
   if note.p # '' then
      body<-1> = ''
      body<-1> = note.p
   end
   begin case
      case pk = 'edit'
         body<-1> = ''
         body<-1> = sysmsg(11665)
         body<-1> = diff.lines
         btn = '&Accept,&Reject'
         dflt = 2                                         ;* a change to a text is never accepted by Enter alone
      case pk = 'action'
         body<-1> = ''
         body<-1> = sysmsg(11647, plabel : (if parg # '' then ' (' : parg : ')' else ''))
         btn = '&Accept,&Reject'
         dflt = (if nav then 1 else 2)
      case pk = 'command'
         body<-1> = ''
         body<-1> = sysmsg(11648)
         body<-1> = '  ' : pcmd
         btn = '&Run,&Cancel'                              ;* (not Reject: its letter would be Run's)
         dflt = 2
      case 1
         btn = '&Close'
         dflt = 1
   end case
   body<-1> = ''
   body<-1> = sysmsg(11634, tok.in, tok.out, ai.prov)
   screen msgbox body title sysmsg(11639) buttons btn default dflt returning bn else bn = 0
   if pk # '' and bn = 1 then
      b = pk : @fm : (if pk = 'action' then pid else (if pk = 'edit' then ed.list else pcmd)) : @fm : parg : @fm : say : @fm : ''
   end else
      b = 'none' : @fm : '' : @fm : '' : @fm : say : @fm : ''
   end
   return

* The model's text to a proposal.  The text is read as ONE JSON object (a first { to the last }, so a code fence round it does no harm); if it is not, it is shown as it is and nothing is
* proposed.  An action is used only if it is exactly one of the ids the app offered; its argument and a command are cleaned; the command is shown, never run here.
read.proposal:
   pk = '' ; pid = '' ; plabel = '' ; parg = '' ; pcmd = '' ; note.p = '' ; say = ''
   f1 = index(atext, '{', 1)
   l1 = 0
   for ci = len(atext) to 1 step -1
      if atext[ci, 1] = '}' then
         l1 = ci
         exit
      end
   next ci
   obj.ok = 0                                              ;* (a collection cannot be compared with a string: the flag says whether obj holds one)
   if f1 > 0 and l1 > f1 then
      obj = jparse(atext[f1, l1 - f1 + 1])
      if not(status()) then obj.ok = 1
   end
   if not(obj.ok) then
      say = atext[1, 600]
      note.p = sysmsg(11651)
      return
   end
   raw = obj{'say'}
   gosub clean
   say = clean.out[1, 600]
   if say = '' then say = ' '
   act = trim(obj{'action'})
   if act # '' and downcase(act) # 'none' then
      found = 0
      for i = 1 to n.acts
         if field(acts<1, i>, ':', 1) = act then
            found = i
            exit
         end
      next i
      if found then
         pk = 'action'
         pid = act
         plabel = trim(acts<1, found>[index(acts<1, found>, ':', 1) + 1, 999])
         raw = obj{'arg'}
         gosub clean
         parg = trim(clean.out)[1, 100]
         if trim(convert('abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789._:/- ', space(65), parg)) # '' then parg = ''
      end else
         note.p = sysmsg(11649, act[1, 40])
      end
   end
   if pk = '' and tbm # '' then gosub read.edits
   if pk = '' and not(no.cmd) then
      raw = obj{'command'}
      gosub clean
      c = trim(clean.out)
      if c # '' then
         if len(c) > 200 or c # raw then
            note.p = sysmsg(11650)
         end else
            pk = 'command'
            pcmd = c
         end
      end
   end
   return

* "edits": a list of {"old", "new"} against the text the model was shown (tbm; tb.raw is the original).  All or none: a set with a single edit that does not fit is ignored whole and
* said so.  What is shown to the person is a diff of EVERY edit in full, and a diff of more than 30 lines is not offered.
read.edits:
   if jtype(obj{'edits'}) # 'array' then return
   epos = '' ; elen = '' ; enew = '' ; ed.n = 0 ; bad.why = ''
   if jtype(obj{'edits/9'}) = 'collection' then bad.why = 'more than 8 edits'      ;* (a collection is never compared with a string; jtype() says 'collection' for an object)
   for ei = 1 to 8
      if bad.why # '' then exit
      if jtype(obj{'edits/' : ei}) # 'collection' then exit
      raw = obj{'edits/' : ei : '/old'}
      gosub clean.nl
      eo = clean.out
      raw = obj{'edits/' : ei : '/new'}
      gosub clean.nl
      en = clean.out
      begin case
         case eo = ''
            bad.why = 'an empty old text'
         case len(en) > 4000
            bad.why = 'a new text over 4000 bytes'
         case 1
            ep = index(tbm, eo, 1)
            begin case
               case ep = 0
                  bad.why = 'old text not found'
               case index(tbm, eo, 2) > 0
                  bad.why = 'old text found more than once'
               case tb.raw[ep, len(eo)] # eo
                  bad.why = 'the text there is not what the model was shown'
               case 1
                  ed.n += 1
                  epos<ed.n> = ep
                  elen<ed.n> = len(eo)
                  enew<ed.n> = en
            end case
      end case
   next ei
   if bad.why = '' and ed.n = 0 then return                  ;* "edits": [] - nothing is proposed, nothing is wrong
   * ascending by position, and no two edits overlap
   if bad.why = '' then
      for i = 1 to ed.n - 1
         for j = i + 1 to ed.n
            if epos<j> < epos<i> then
               t = epos<i> ; epos<i> = epos<j> ; epos<j> = t
               t = elen<i> ; elen<i> = elen<j> ; elen<j> = t
               t = enew<i> ; enew<i> = enew<j> ; enew<j> = t
            end
         next j
      next i
      for i = 1 to ed.n - 1
         if epos<i> + elen<i> > epos<i + 1> then bad.why = 'two edits overlap'
      next i
   end
   if bad.why # '' then
      note.p = sysmsg(11660, bad.why)
      return
   end
   * the diff, in full
   diff.lines = ''
   ed.list = ''
   dl = 0
   for k = 1 to ed.n
      ep = epos<k>
      line.no = tb.first
      if ep > 1 then line.no = tb.first + count(tb.raw[1, ep - 1], nl)
      diff.lines<-1> = sysmsg(11658, k, ed.n, line.no)
      eo = tb.raw[ep, elen<k>]
      for j = 1 to dcount(eo, nl)
         diff.lines<-1> = '- ' : field(eo, nl, j)[1, wrapw - 6]
         dl += 1
      next j
      en = enew<k>
      if en # '' then
         for j = 1 to dcount(en, nl)
            diff.lines<-1> = '+ ' : field(en, nl, j)[1, wrapw - 6]
            dl += 1
         next j
      end
      ed.list<1, -1> = ep : @sm : elen<k> : @sm : en
   next k
   if dl > 30 then
      note.p = sysmsg(11659, dl)
      return
   end
   pk = 'edit'
   return

* The text as the model is shown it, ONE BYTE FOR ONE: plain ASCII and the line feed as they are, a tab as a blank, anything else as ?
map1:
   map.out = ''
   for ci = 1 to len(raw)
      ch = raw[ci, 1]
      sq = seq(ch)
      begin case
         case sq >= 32 and sq <= 126
            map.out := ch
         case sq = 10
            map.out := ch
         case sq = 9
            map.out := ' '
         case 1
            map.out := '?'
      end case
   next ci
   return

* The model's text for an edit: plain ASCII and the line feed; a tab or a return becomes a blank; anything else is dropped
clean.nl:
   clean.out = ''
   for ci = 1 to len(raw)
      sq = seq(raw[ci, 1])
      begin case
         case sq >= 32 and sq <= 126
            clean.out := raw[ci, 1]
         case sq = 10
            clean.out := raw[ci, 1]
         case sq = 9 or sq = 13
            clean.out := ' '
      end case
   next ci
   return

* Plain ASCII only: a control character, a mark or a byte above 126 is dropped (a line feed, a return or a tab becomes a space)
clean:
   clean.out = ''
   for ci = 1 to len(raw)
      sq = seq(raw[ci, 1])
      if sq >= 32 and sq <= 126 then
         clean.out := raw[ci, 1]
      end else
         if sq = 10 or sq = 13 or sq = 9 then clean.out := ' '
      end
   next ci
   return

end

